  "helper_contract": {
    "api": "decode_dispatch(rom: bytes, root: int) -> dict; pure, no IO or project imports",
    "derivation": [
      "Only exact Thumb-1 families listed. root even and full 26-byte range in ROM. Both literal addresses = aligned(source+4) + imm8*4, 4-byte aligned in ROM and no overlap with code/table/each other.",
      "first literal is an opaque RAM state base value, output raw word; second literal is ROM table address (GBA 0x08000000 base). Table length = (CMP imm8 + 1) * 4. SUB uses 32-bit wrap; unsigned BHI exits when index > CMP imm8. Reject if subtract+maximum >255; all slots must have a real u8 command witness.",
      "BHI signed target outside prefix/data. LSL is exactly r0,r0,#2; table load adds r1 to r0 then loads u32 then MOV pc,r0 retaining Thumb mode. It is not BX; table targets must be even ROM addresses with mode thumb; reject any prefix/literal/table target.",
      "Return every prefix node offset/size/raw_hex; two literal_bindings triples[source,target,rawhex]; state_base_value; state_pointer_field_offset; command_field_offset; subtract; maximum_index; default_target; table_range; table_sha256; ordered table_entries {slot_index,entry_offset,raw_pointer,target,mode}; all256 input_domain {command,index_u32,slot_index or null,target}.",
      "Output keys exactly: root,prefix_range,instructions,literal_bindings,state_base_value,state_pointer_field_offset,command_field_offset,subtract,maximum_index,default_target,table_range,table_sha256,table_entries,input_domain. Integers offsets; mode string thumb; no natural or lifecycle claims.",
      "Real expected root0x7DCB8, literal state0x02026BE0 + field0xC4, command+4, subtract36 max19 default0x7DD42, table[0x7DCDC,0x7DD2C), table targets DD2C,DD2C,DD42,DD34,DD34,DD42 fourteen times,DD3C. All20 slots must be enumerated.",
      "Use TDD before implementation, real oracle and relocated synthetic case with different subtract/bound/literal addresses/targets. Reject BLS, wrong flag producer/scale/register/PC-write mode, 32-bit or out-of-range table pointers, odd targets, truncation, duplicate or overlapping data ranges. Only parent integrates source/owner/full-ROM scan/downstream CFG."
    ],
    "pattern_halfwords": [
